[2026-04-08 07:26:10] [pre-recon] [LLM] Turn 173: {"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CCr36sW72FddkMsvj9ergF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"XSS/Injection Sink Hunter","prompt":"You are a security specialist focused on finding XSS and injection sinks. Analyze this Node.js freelance marketplace application (HireFlow/WebVulnBench).\n\n**CONTEXT:** This is a Node.js Express backend with a React (Vite) frontend in client/src/. The backend serves the React SPA. Key backend modules are in src/ with subdirectories: auth, users, gigs, contracts, payments, messaging, reviews, disputes, notifications, admin, integrations, middleware, utils, config, models.\n\n**Tasks:**\n\n### Backend (Server-Side Injection Sinks):\n1. Read ALL service files in src/*/service.js or src/*/*.service.js - find:\n   - SQL injection: raw SQL queries, string interpolation in queries, whereRaw, knex.raw\n   - NoSQL injection: MongoDB $where, string-built queries, unsanitized operators\n   - Command injection: exec, spawn, child_process usage\n   - Template injection: any server-side template rendering with user data\n   - Deserialization: JSON.parse of user input, eval(), Function(), vm.runInNewContext\n2. Read src/utils/pdf.js - analyze HTML template generation for server-side XSS via Puppeteer\n3. Read ALL controller files for unvalidated user input passed to services\n4. Check for eval(), Function(), setTimeout/setInterval with string args\n\n### Frontend (Client-Side XSS Sinks):\n5. Read ALL files in client/src/ - search for:\n   - dangerouslySetInnerHTML usage in React components\n   - innerHTML, outerHTML assignments\n   - document.write, document.writeln\n   - jQuery DOM manipulation (.html(), .append() with user data)\n   - eval(), Function(), setTimeout with strings\n   - URL manipulation (location.href, window.open with user data)\n   - DOM-based XSS via URL params (useSearchParams, window.location)\n6. Check for any unescaped rendering of user-provided content (reviews, messages, gig descriptions, profile data)\n\n**Output Format:** For EACH sink found, provide:\n- Exact file path with line numbers\n- The vulnerable code snippet\n- The render context (HTML body, attribute, JavaScript, URL, CSS)\n- Whether it's network-reachable (can be triggered by a request)\n- Severity assessment\n- Attack scenario\n\nBe exhaustive. Check every file in client/src/ and every service/controller in src/.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}
