[2026-04-08 08:45:18] [auth-exploit] [LLM] Turn 146: {"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The victim's session after login is empty (no session cookie set in response), even though we sent the attacker's session. This is unusual. Let me investigate more.\n\nActually wait - when `cookie.secure: false` and we're accessing via HTTP (which we are), the cookie SHOULD be sent. But the response didn't include a Set-Cookie header. Let me debug this more.\n\nActually, thinking about it again: when the victim logs in WITH the attacker's session cookie, express-session finds the existing session in Redis (session belongs to the attacker, userId = attacker.id). The login sets `req.session.userId = victim.id`, which overwrites the attacker's userId. \n\nSince the session already exists and was modified, express-session saves it but doesn't issue a new Set-Cookie header because the session ID itself hasn't changed. So session S_A now contains userId = victim.id instead of the attacker's ID, meaning when the attacker uses S_A, they're authenticated as the victim. Let me verify the attacker can actually access the victim's account with this hijacked session.","signature":""}
